<!--Post: 832--><!--Time: 1093024912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST832"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 20, 2004 - 11:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->According to rumor the letter from BTK last May had this:  <BR> <BR>1. A SERIAL KILLER ________  <BR>2. DAWN  <BR>3. FETISH  <BR>4. FANTASY WORLD  <BR>5. THE SEARCH BEGINS  <BR>6. BTK&#39;S HAUNTS  <BR>7. PJ&#39;S  <BR>8. MO-ID RUSE  <BR>9. KITS  <BR>10. TREASURED MEMORIES  <BR>11. FINAL CURTAIN CALL  <BR>12. DUSK  <BR>13. WILL THERE MORE?  <BR> <BR>This is a parody off the table of contents from the CrimeLibrary. &#40;<a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve</a> d/btk/index_1.html?sect=4&#41;  <BR>They had a story on the BTK with the contents reading as this:  <BR> <BR>1.All American City  <BR>2.A Chilling Discovery  <BR>3.Bind Them, Torture Them, Kill Them  <BR>4.Different Worlds Collide  <BR>5.Vanishing Act  <BR>6.Ghost Busters  <BR>7.The Next Step  <BR>8.Cold Case Squad  <BR>9.Profile  <BR>10.Aftermath  <BR>11.BTK Returns  <BR>12.Bibliography  <BR>13.The Author  <BR> <BR> <BR>As we can see the Police confirmed BTK&#39;s Chapter 7&#39;s PJ, but what I find intersting is the 8th chapter. Of all the chapter&#39;s these two are the most interesting because of their encrypted letters.  <BR> <BR>The 8th is SUPPOSEDLY written as MO-ID RUSE  <BR> <BR>What ID could mean is the revealing of his ID use. MO may mean the state &#34;Missouri&#34;. MO is also another word for &#34;Mail Order&#34; &#40;check out dictionary.com&#41;, &#34;Money Order&#34;, or &#34;modusoperandi&#34;  <BR> <BR>Modusoperandi means &#34;A method of operating or functioning.&#34; or &#34;A person&#39;s manner of working.&#34;  <BR> <BR>Indeed all these meanings for MO is VERY VERY VERY tantilizing. If he had to choose one abbreviation that would confuse people. MO is it.  <BR> <BR>Now then, the word &#34;ruse&#34; has many intentions. He could mean that this Modusoperandi ID was a ruse to get into houses, or that his Missouri ID was a ruse.  <BR> <BR>OR he could be saying that this revelation of his &#34;fake ID&#34; scheme could be a ruse to the police and that he gets into buildings a DIFFERENT way.  <BR> <BR>All in all a very interesting and weird devlopment. <BR> <BR>&#40;i already posted this in another topic, but thought I should post it again as its own topic&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 832-->
<!--Post: 833--><!--Time: 1093025349-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST833"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 20, 2004 - 11:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Other possible ID meanings: <BR> <BR>Idaho <BR>Indonesia <BR>Identification <BR>Intelligence Department <BR>Irvine Dataflow <BR>Internet-Draft <BR>Idem &#40;Something that has been mentioned previously; the same&#41; <BR>inner diameter <BR>inside diameter <BR>internal diameter <BR>intradermal <BR>Contraction of I had. <BR>Contraction of I would. <BR> <BR>Id: In Freudian theory, the division of the psyche that is totally unconscious and serves as the source of instinctual impulses and demands for immediate satisfaction of primitive needs. <BR> <BR>Id: a skin rash that is an allergic reaction to an agent causing an infection <BR> <BR>ID: A symbol used for the dose of an infectious organism required to produce infection in 50 percent of the experimental subject. <BR> <BR>Id: A small fresh-water cyprinoid fish &#40;Leuciscus idus or Idus idus&#41; of Europe. A domesticated variety, colored like the goldfish, is called orfe in Germany.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 833-->
<!--Post: 834--><!--Time: 1093025589-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST834"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 20, 2004 - 11:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Other MO meanings: <BR> <BR>Macao <BR>molybdenum <BR>medical officer <BR>month <BR> <BR>Other meanings of Ruse <BR> <BR>Ruse: A city of northeast Bulgaria on the Danube River south of Bucharest, Romania. Founded as a Roman fortress, it is today a major port and industrial center. Population: 193,000. <BR> <BR>Ruse: A crafty stratagem; a subterfuge. &#40;most likely&#41; <BR> <BR>AS WRITTEN AT DICTIOANRY.COM: <BR> <BR>ruse <BR> <BR>n : a deceptive maneuver &#40;especially to avoid capture&#41; [syn: artifice]<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 834-->
<!--Post: 1017--><!--Time: 1094825700-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1017"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Will_graham<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Will_graham<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->9-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, September 10, 2004 - 7:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have wondered about the I.D. ruse. Does that mean the way he got I.D.&#39;s? If so I have a theory. I think he may have been a janitor. He would have access to the books in the library, could make copies, and be able to steal I.D&#39;s all without being detected. That would also help him in learing to clean his tracks. I am just an amateur slueth so maybe someone can set me straight on this one.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
